<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.6.4: Finding the Missing Numbers in Pairs of Equivalent Expressions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02184</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.6.4: Finding the Missing Numbers in Pairs of Equivalent Expressions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9d312361-64af-475d-bf89-8a796f820ec1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Cool Down Activity</title>
<para>The problems below consist of pairs of equivalent expressions: one in standard form and the other in factored form. Note that the leading coefficients on the quadratic terms are all 1.</para>
<para>Find the missing numbers.</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2 \;+\) __\(x\;+\) __ and \((x + 1)(x + 17)\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the missing numbers.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>18 and 17, respectively. The completed expression is \(x^2+18x +17\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2+9x +14\) and \((x + 2)(x\; +\) __\()\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the missing number.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 7. The completed expression is \((x + 2)(x + 7)\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2−7x +10\) and \((x − 2)(x\; −\) __\()\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the missing number.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 5. The completed expression is \((x − 2)(x − 5)\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>\(x^2−9x +20\) and \((x\; −\) __)\((x\; −\) __\()\)</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the missing numbers.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para> 4 and 5. The completed expression is \((x − 4)(x − 5)\).</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
